2 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419682 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419682 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419682 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419682 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419682 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "80639a3b-2c96-57ee-bd01-981e0851478b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419683 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419683 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140453" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419683 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419683 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419683 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "426fab7e-1490-581a-8c87-fe143e595ca4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419683 #edb/ref 1074 "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419687 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419687 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0b2e1e0a-a93e-5b2b-ba4a-b6011da00e9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419687 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419688 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419688 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1b0f643e-dd6c-5eaf-875c-1b54d4c6e171" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419688 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419689 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419689 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "49084fac-fe76-5f2f-8b13-058b89e81921" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419689 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419690 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419690 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9a18e940-4aa2-5db0-8cbe-98d6ec06c6cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419690 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419691 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bf368b08-5b21-5ea2-9201-b8d34ec52b51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419691 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186448614 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186448614 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186448614 #edb/r